[{"id":"VRCE-4-4-1","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":4,"verse":1,"english":"Hearing those words (of Rāma) and learning his amicable feeling (in relation to Sugrīva) as also, seeing that Rāma was willing to assist Sugrīva, Hanuman, getting exceedingly delighted, remembered Sugrīva.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.79,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-4-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4004001","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fa221789c95c8b24b8f7f605e0c26b74c884878781c8d689879dc4fa6ada8054","compact":"32121624f7d5c0ac4668e8c1e3f714765fe8ce479f815ee7f17cbb1cdc1486c5","nasal":"32121624f7d5c0ac4668e8c1e3f714765fe8ce479f815ee7f17cbb1cdc1486c5"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-4-2","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":4,"verse":2,"english":"Since this one of successful acts has been come by and also this business is in hand, the high-souled Sugrīva will most probably obtain the monarchy.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.985,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-4-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4004002","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"671ae6403db719e38cd92a21a41366a2c38f45a113542b8d235eadef4561a392","compact":"956b1cad8ba37997c8009af298e213fc77406a13fbf24487b8afdaf1bf1873a8","nasal":"956b1cad8ba37997c8009af298e213fc77406a13fbf24487b8afdaf1bf1873a8"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-4-3","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":4,"verse":3,"english":"Then transported with joy, that foremost of monkeys, Hanumān, in these words, replied to Rāma, deft in speech, saying,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.678,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-4-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4004003","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6468fd92e531d6d53bbfb06e4dd169849e0e1e