, famous among men.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.5,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-4-6","DUTT-4-4-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4004006","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e88e7809ce5e8f5ad33467c09ef87413f7cb0cf618e6a242dc2cb59e78c29b75","compact":"a761f5555156dab5e636863ee6b695e51dd3a853783ca81ac9b2e697797071fb","nasal":"3bbd6b81923193e40fc6a62f372ac4b26d8988621d4f6fd92898f403a0bcd84d"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-4-7","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":4,"verse":7,"english":"He is the refuge of all creatures, and competent to carry out the injunctions of his father. The eldest son of Dasaratha, he is foremost of all his sons in merit.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.833,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-4-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4004007","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5f708186246022c0e298f4248bfcd63c29f1899701d0519d8ac640ad4e7e8ba2","compact":"901fbe6e1598faba624b62490da4b59bdc3f2c2f9cebd467813f8e0fe0d540b3","nasal":"901fbe6e1598faba624b62490da4b59bdc3f2c2f9cebd467813f8e0fe0d540b3"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-4-8","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":4,"verse":8,"english":"And, O highly exalted one, this one of subdued senses is followed by his wife Sītā even as the decline of day the exceedingly effulgent Sun is followed by (his spouse) Splendour.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.44,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-4-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4004008","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0c6a96965f1dc3d8bff2d9df4f33ff06b5eb095499ea25029f2a233f534b9c3d","compact":"2d79bdb14dbb449b230f775cc2bda009cde5c7baa82682cdedc50b9cea50e3b2","nasal":"2d79bdb14dbb449b230f775cc2bda009cde5c7baa82682cdedc50b9cea50e3b2"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-4-9","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":4,"verse":9,"english":"I am the younger brother of this one endued with gratitude and of various lore. Subdued by his virtues, I, Laksimana by name, have dedicated myself to his service.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-4-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4004009","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"34eb3179982c1836cf12a905cca62ec513b02a8bc98262b37833232af22a9b6e","compact":"5297e05dbc11eb8e9ff34288d1a136499d8a6a8ef642567454a5c3b82bac271d","nasal":"5297e05dbc11eb8e9ff34288d1a136499d8a6a8ef642567454a5c3b82bac271d"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-4-10","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":4,"verse":10,"english":"Worthy of happiness, homage, and intent upon the welfare of all beings, deprived of wealth and living in the forest, he has his wife carried off by a Rākşasa, wearing shapes at will. Nor have we yet (been able) to ascertain who is that Rākşasa that has carried off his wife.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.567,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-4-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4004010","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3700a884b1585e3063c7c0e9a90611c099f1ccba1c16625ea44969a099c4071b","compact":"1f8fe09804199307c0a419869042dab0969027e2f7f079729b914a6fc0be3f96","nasal":"1f8fe09804199307c0a419869042dab0969027e2f7f079729b914a6fc0be3f96"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-4-11","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":4,"verse":11,"english":"Worthy of happiness, homage, and intent upon the welfare of all beings, deprived of wealth and living in the forest, he has his wife carried off by a Rākşasa, wearing shapes at will. Nor have we yet (been able) to ascertain who is that Rākşasa that has carried off his wife.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.898,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-4-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4004011","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"af9a7aaddbd84068ef60553a15592adcfa5b262a87a969ff3c0122497a280714","compact":"5166f7f5b4f6bb71100e5cd49dfbbb812eee7adb7b7697d74c036d8dd03a89e4","nasal":"5166f7f5b4f6bb71100e5cd49dfbbb812eee7adb7b7697d74c036d8dd03a89e4"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-4-12","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":4,"verse":12,"english":"A son of Diti named Danu, had, by virtue of an imprecation, undergone Raksasa-hood. He it is who had related to us all about the capable Sugrīva.—That exceedingly puissant one shall have a knowledge of the ravisher of your wife? Having said this, Danu beaming (with a halo) went to heaven.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.815,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-4-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4004012","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f7589974e2224bbbb3eb4445a74c1f2a769a35645c1273f9a6e2b7f7e68a78dd","compact":"a931c5f0f9e9010be5566f25d380d6f9ff8667380f5e5b30841c0060ba0632e1","nasal":"a931c5f0f9e9010be5566f25d380d6f9ff8667380f5e5b30841c0060ba0632e1"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-4-13","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":4,"verse":13,"english":"A son of Diti named Danu, had, by virtue of an imprecation, undergone Raksasa-hood. He it is who had related to us all about the capable Sugrīva.—That exceedingly puissant one shall have a knowledge of the ravisher of your wife? Having said this, Danu beaming (with a halo) went to heaven.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.761,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-4-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4004013","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8200a313dbfdb30a80f6b862e799145d39ed2224addab0bbe2b8496